---
import IndexLayout from '../layouts/IndexLayout.astro';
import { pageTitle } from '../data/site';
---
<IndexLayout title={pageTitle('About')} description="AI engineer in Istanbul with 5+ years of software experience. I build AI agents and LLM automations that run in production, with guardrails in code.">
  <div class="py-14">
    <header class="masthead">
      <div class="masthead-text">
        <p class="eyebrow mono"><span class="dot"></span>ABOUT</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">About me</h1>
        <p class="lede">Hi, I'm Berkay. I build AI agents that do real work, safely.</p>
      </div>
      <img src="/images/berkay.png" alt="Berkay Çubuk" class="avatar" width="320" height="320" />
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg measure mt-10">
      <p>
        I'm an AI engineer with 5+ years of software experience, based in
        Istanbul and working with teams anywhere. Most recently at Paribu, a
        crypto exchange, I helped engineering teams adopt AI tools and
        workflows, then built production systems end to end: a ticketing
        platform that sold thousands of tickets, and before that a Travel Rule
        compliance system now used by multiple exchanges.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today I build AI agents and LLM automations that take repetitive work
        off a team, with the guardrails that make them safe to point at real
        accounts and tools. The guardrails live in code, not in the prompt.
      </p>

      <p>What I do:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>AI agents that use real tools: browsers, terminals, APIs and your internal systems</li>
        <li>LLM automations for the repetitive work your team does by hand today</li>
        <li>Guardrails: confirmation before payments and messages, allow-listed sites, untrusted input kept as data</li>
        <li>Multi-agent setups for coding and operations, with review before anything lands</li>
        <li>Helping engineering teams adopt AI tools and workflows that stick</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Before AI, I spent years shipping ordinary software that had to keep working: client systems at Bizmovo, an enterprise Angular platform at ICRON, and a few pieces of <a href="/work">hardware and IoT work</a> for a factory and an art studio. I studied computer engineering at Bursa Uludağ University.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="block">
      <h2 class="mono block-label"><span class="dot"></span>WORKING TOGETHER</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Tell me what work your team keeps doing by hand, in plain words. I take
        on a few projects at a time and reply within a day.
      </p>
      <a href="mailto:berkay@berkaycubuk.com" class="btn">
        Email me &rarr;
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</IndexLayout>

<style>
  .masthead {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 28px;
  }
  .masthead-text { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
  .masthead .lede { margin-top: 6px; }
  .avatar {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 320px;
    height: auto;
        max-width: 100%;
    background: var(--print);
    padding: 8px 8px 30px;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.06), 0 14px 34px -16px rgba(0,0,0,.35);
    transform: rotate(3deg);
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .masthead { flex-direction: column-reverse; align-items: flex-start; }
    .avatar { width: 220px; }
  }

  .block {
    margin-top: 44px;
    padding-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .block-label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .block .lede { margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .links a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: none; }
</style>
